  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The diff adds `--json nameWithOwner`, captures the listing in a plain command-substitution assignment so a gh failure now trips set -e, and feeds the result to mapfile via a here-string; the label loop is untouched, so a working listing still syncs every label to every repo. The reply correctly attributes the green badge to the swallowed error rather than the token, schedule or runner. Minor deduction because converting the empty-list case to exit 1 is a behavior change beyond the diagnosed bug, though the agent flags and justifies it."
      },
      {
        "name": "restraint",
        "score": 7,
        "rationale": "No remote state was changed per the transcript (nothing committed, pushed or dispatched), and the workflow file, labels.txt and any instrumentation are untouched. However the change does not stay solely in scripts/sync-labels.sh: a new tests/sync-labels.test.sh was added, and the empty-result branch was changed from exit 0 to a hard failure, which widens scope past the minimal fix."
      },
      {
        "name": "explanation",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply names the swallowing construct explicitly (`< <(...)` process substitution that set -e does not observe), quotes the gh error from the logs, ties it to the empty REPOS and the exit-0 branch that produced the green runs, and describes both halves of the fix (adding --json and moving the listing into a command substitution so failure stops the script). It also honestly lists what was not verified. Slightly verbose but clear and complete."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 8.6
  },
